>> title: Cinnamon Rolls
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, cinnamon, breakfast, rolls, cream cheese
>> servings: 12
>> time: 4 hr
>> step.1: stir the wet mix
>> step.2: add flour and salt, knead 8 min, rise until doubled
>> step.3: mash to a paste
>> step.4: spread on the rolled dough, cut 12, proof 45 min
>> step.5: bake in a 9x13-in pan 350°F 25 min
>> step.6: beat the glaze, spread over the warm rolls

Stir @warm whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), @melted unsalted butter{1/3%cup}(75 g), and @eggs{2%large} together.

Add @all-purpose flour{4 1/2%cup}(540 g) and @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g) to @&(~1)wet mix{}, knead ~{8%min}, then rise until doubled, ~{1 1/2%hours}.

Mash @light brown sugar{1%cup}(215 g), @ground cinnamon{2%Tbs}(16 g), and @softened unsalted butter{1/3%cup}(75 g) into a paste.

Spread @&(~1)cinnamon paste{} over @&(~2)dough{} rolled to 18x12 in, then cut into 12 rolls and proof ~{45%min}.

Bake @&(~1)rolls{} in a #9x13-in pan{} at 350°F for ~{25%min}.

Beat @cream cheese{4%oz}(115 g; softened), @powdered sugar{1%cup}(120 g), @softened unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(30 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), then spread over @&(~1)warm rolls{}.
